  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 342 PM CDT Fri Jul 24 2026\n\nHeat and humidity return starting Saturday and will persist \nthrough early next week. We issued a Heat Advisory for Saturday \nover most of the Northland and an Extreme Heat Watch for Sunday.\nAdditional heat headlines may be needed Monday and Tuesday.\n\nIn addition to the heat Saturday, there is a risk of a storm or\ntwo breaking through the cap. In the event storms develop, they\nwill be capable of large hail and damaging wind. As of this \nafternoon, the risk of storms is less than 10% for any given \nlocation.\n\nSunday will bring another potential for showers and storms, \nsome of which may be severe. An elevated mixed layer is forecast\nto advect eastward over the region which will limit storm \npotential initially. Strong heating beneath the cap will result \nin an area of 3000-4000 J/kg of MUCAPE. There is a small chance \na few storms may break through the cap in the afternoon. The \nmore likely evolution will be storms developing near a cold \nfront in southern Manitoba and northeast North Dakota and moving\ninto north-central and central Minnesota during the evening. If\nstorms form in the afternoon, very large hail and damaging \nwinds are possible. With the later round of storms, damaging \nwinds will be the main threat.\n\nTemperatures cool a bit behind the front Monday. Heat headlines\nmay be needed once again. For the remainder of next week, \ntemperatures will be in the 80s and low 90s until Friday. \nAdditional heat headlines may be needed. There will also be \nperiodic chances of rain and storms, mainly focused Wednesday \nnight and beyond.",
